## Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files:**

1. **src/App.jsx**
   - Added import for `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/react`
   - Integrated `<Analytics />` component within the ResumeProvider context
   - This ensures analytics tracking is active throughout the application

2. **src/main.jsx**
   - Removed deprecated `inject()` function approach
   - Cleaned up unused `@vercel/analytics` import
   - Simplified to use the component-based approach per latest docs

### Implementation Details

The project already had `@vercel/analytics` (v2.0.1) installed in package.json. The implementation was updated from the older `inject()` method to the newer React component approach as recommended in the official documentation.

The `<Analytics />` component was placed inside the App component's ResumeProvider wrapper, ensuring it has access to the React context and will track all page views and interactions across the application.

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully (vite build)
✅ No errors or warnings introduced
✅ Analytics component properly imported and integrated
✅ Following React/Vite best practices from official Vercel docs

### Next Steps

To fully activate analytics:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify tracking in browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/view` requests

The implementation is production-ready and follows the latest Vercel Analytics guidelines.
